{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/math\/customdimensions"]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"Math"}],"title":"Custom Dimensions and Units"},"kind":"article","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CustomDimensions","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extend "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"type":"text","text":" with your own physical dimensions and units—currency, points, gameplay metrics, or anything else your app measures."}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Extending-the-Framework","title":"Extending the Framework"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"type":"text","text":" ships with a comprehensive set of base dimensions ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/length"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/time"},{"type":"text","text":", and friends) and derived dimensions ("},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/speed"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/energy"},{"type":"text","text":", and more). These cover physics and everyday measurement, but your app almost certainly measures things that aren’t in the SI system too: money, hit points, ingredients, resource points, users, and so on."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The good news: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension"},{"type":"text","text":" is an open system. Because a dimension is "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"just a dictionary of exponent powers"}]},{"type":"text","text":", you can describe any dimension you can imagine at runtime."}]},{"anchor":"Define-a-Custom-Dimension","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Define a Custom Dimension"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension"},{"type":"text","text":" with a dictionary of exponent identifiers. Each key is a dimension name and each value is its power:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["import Math","","\/\/ A dimension for money, with a single base exponent.","let usdDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"USD\": 1])","","\/\/ A dimension for \"users\", used later in per-user metrics.","let userDimension = PhysicalDimension(exponents: [\"user\": 1])"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can build compound custom dimensions with the same arithmetic used"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"internally: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"+"},{"type":"text","text":" multiplies dimensions, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"type":"text","text":" divides them, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"*"},{"type":"text","text":" with an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"type":"text","text":" raises a dimension to a power:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let revenuePerUser = usdDimension - userDimension   \/\/ [\"USD\": 1, \"user\": -1]"]},{"anchor":"Define-Custom-Units","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Define Custom Units"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom dimensions don’t have a compile-time type, so use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/unknown"},{"type":"text","text":" as the type-level parameter and "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/NamedUnit"},{"type":"text","text":" to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"create units. Pass a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/LinearConverter"},{"type":"text","text":" (for a simple scale) or an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/OffsetConverter"},{"type":"text","text":" (for a scale plus an offset) to handle conversions:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let usdUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"$\",","    dimension: usdDimension,","    converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.0)",")","","\/\/ EUR is defined relative to the same base dimension.","let eurUnit = NamedUnit<MathDimension.unknown>(","    symbol: \"€\",","    dimension: usdDimension,","    converter: LinearConverter(coefficient: 1.09)",")"]},{"type":"aside","style":"tip","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Keep the same "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PhysicalDimension"},{"type":"text","text":" value (here "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"usdDimension"},{"type":"text","text":") for every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"unit in a family. The framework only converts between units whose dimensions"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"match, so sharing the exact same value makes your money interchangeable."}]}],"name":"Tip"},{"anchor":"Convert-Between-Custom-Units","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Convert Between Custom Units"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom units convert exactly like the built-in ones:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let walletInEur = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: eurUnit)","let walletInUsd = walletInEur.converted(to: usdUnit)","","print(walletInUsd.value) \/\/ 109.0"]},{"anchor":"Combine-Custom-Units-with-Built-In-Ones","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Combine Custom Units with Built-In Ones"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Custom dimensions participate in dimensional arithmetic too. Here a currency"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension combines with the built-in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/time"},{"type":"text","text":" dimension:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let hourlyRate = Quantity(value: 50.0, unit: usdUnit) \/ Quantity(value: 1.0, unit: Units.hour)","","print(hourlyRate.value)          \/\/ 50.0","print(hourlyRate.unit.dimension) \/\/ [\"USD\": 1, \"time\": -1]","print(hourlyRate.unit.symbol)    \/\/ \"($\/h)\""]},{"anchor":"Use-the-Currency-Dimension","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Use the Currency Dimension"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your custom dimension happens to be currency, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Math"},{"type":"text","text":" already defines a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/currency"},{"type":"text","text":" dimension and a built-in library of world"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"currencies (and cryptocurrencies) in "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units"},{"type":"text","text":". Currency units automatically"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"place their symbol before the value when formatting:"}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let gift = Quantity(value: 100.0, unit: Units.usd)","print(gift.formatted()) \/\/ \"$100.00\"","","\/\/ Resolve units from ISO 4217 codes at runtime.","if let currency = Units.currency(for: \"SEK\") {","    print(currency.symbol) \/\/ \"kr\"","}"]},{"anchor":"Whats-Next","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"What’s Next?"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn how to lock custom units into a compile-time dimension in"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Explore "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units"},{"type":"text","text":" to see the breadth of units provided out of the box."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math"]]},"references":{"doc://Math/documentation/Math/LinearConverter":{"title":"LinearConverter","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/LinearConverter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/UnitConverter"},{"type":"text","text":" that scales values by a fixed coefficient."}],"url":"\/documentation\/math\/linearconverter","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinearConverter","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinearConverter","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/NamedUnit":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/NamedUnit","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NamedUnit","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/namedunit","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"NamedUnit","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"NamedUnit","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A unit with a fixed symbol and dimension, parameterized by its compile-time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension type."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/PhysicalDimension/speed":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"speed"},{"kind":"text","text":": `Self`"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/physicaldimension\/speed","role":"symbol","title":"speed","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/speed","abstract":[{"text":"The dimension of speed (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"length \/ time"},{"text":").","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/PhysicalDimension/time":{"title":"time","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/time","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The dimension of time (SI base unit: second)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/math\/physicaldimension\/time","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"time"},{"kind":"text","text":": `Self`"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/PhysicalDimension/length":{"title":"length","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/length","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The dimension of length (SI base unit: meter)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/math\/physicaldimension\/length","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"length"},{"kind":"text","text":": `Self`"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/PhysicalDimension/currency":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"currency"},{"kind":"text","text":": `Self`"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/physicaldimension\/currency","role":"symbol","title":"currency","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/currency","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The dimension of currency."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/UnitConverter":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnitConverter"}],"title":"UnitConverter","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/UnitConverter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"UnitConverter"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/unitconverter","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type that converts numeric values between a unit and the base unit of its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"dimension."}]},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/PhysicalDimension/energy":{"title":"energy","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension\/energy","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The dimension of energy ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"force × length"},{"type":"text","text":", SI unit: joule)."}],"url":"\/documentation\/math\/physicaldimension\/energy","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"energy"},{"kind":"text","text":": `Self`"}],"role":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/CompileTimeSafety":{"kind":"article","url":"\/documentation\/math\/compiletimesafety","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/CompileTimeSafety","title":"Compile-Time Dimension Type Safety","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Use generic constraints to make sure your APIs only ever receive the right kind of quantity."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/MathDimension/unknown":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"unknown"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/mathdimension\/unknown","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"unknown"}],"title":"MathDimension.unknown","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/MathDimension\/unknown","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The compile-time dimension type used for dimensions that don’t have a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"static type, such as custom dimensions created at runtime."}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/Units":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Units"}],"kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/units","role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Units"}],"title":"Units","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/Units","abstract":[{"text":"A namespace of ready-made units for every dimension in the framework.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/PhysicalDimension":{"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"PhysicalDimension"}],"role":"symbol","title":"PhysicalDimension","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/PhysicalDimension","url":"\/documentation\/math\/physicaldimension","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A type representing a physical dimension as a canonical dictionary of base SI dimension exponents."}],"type":"topic","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PhysicalDimension"}]},"doc://Math/documentation/Math":{"title":"Math","role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/math","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Perform type-safe dimensional analysis and unit conversion in your Swift app."}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math","type":"topic"},"doc://Math/documentation/Math/OffsetConverter":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/OffsetConverter","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"OffsetConverter"}],"role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/math\/offsetconverter","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"OffsetConverter"}],"title":"OffsetConverter","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/Math\/documentation\/Math\/UnitConverter","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that scales values by a coefficient and adds a constant"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"offset."}],"kind":"symbol","type":"topic"}}}